  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-control-infrastructure.html#constructing-the-form-data-set\r\n\r\n> 2. Let the form data set be a list of name-value-type tuples, initially empty.\r\n\r\nThe ```type``` is used only to check \"it's file or not\" in each of form encodings.\r\nI think we can simplify specifications by changing the checks to something like \"if the value is a file ...\"\r\n\r\nThis affects URL specification and XHR specification as well as HTML specification.\r\nhttps://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-urlencoded-serializer\r\nhttps://xhr.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-formdata-entry\r\n\r\nThis change should not affect UA behavior.\r\n",
